    "scenario": "BGP AS Path Access List",
    "goals": "• Configure EBGP between all directly connected routers.\n  AS {{as1}}: {{router2_name}}\n  AS {{as2}}: {{router3_name}}\n  AS {{as3}}: {{router1_name}}\n  AS {{as4}}: {{router4_name}}\n• You are only allowed to use AS Path Access-Lists to complete the following filtering tasks.\n• Advertise the loopback0 and loopback1 interfaces on all routers in BGP.\n• Ensure AS {{as1}} does not become a transit AS: router {{router2_name}} must not advertise prefixes learned from AS {{as4}} towards AS {{as2}}, and must not advertise prefixes learned from AS {{as2}} towards AS {{as4}}.\n• Configure router {{router1_name}} so it doesn’t advertise any prefixes from AS {{as2}} towards AS {{as4}}.\n• Configure AS {{as4}} so it doesn’t accept any prefixes originated by AS {{as1}}.",
